From 5f2e14a6303c6d3d37f8a4ecf321d7562a0872f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:53:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] robo: batch matching, date/batch filters, per-slab
 production date, reports redesign, hourly chart, styled exports

Nine related changes across Robo Reports, Downloads and Entry:

- Batch numbers normalize so D1372 = d1372 = D-1372 = 1372, but A-1248 != D-1248,
  across every search and filter.
- Reports and Downloads gain a Date Range option (All / Date Wise / Date Range;
  the old "Random Date" is now "Date Wise") and an independent Batch Number filter
  that ANDs with the date.
- Filters are reordered (Batch first, Production Date second) and the page opens on
  the latest batch.
- Per-slab Production Date for batches that run past midnight: a later slab can move
  to the next day without renumbering earlier slabs; the new date carries forward.
  Adds a nullable RoboProductionRecord.productionDate column
  (scripts/0047-robo-slab-production-date.sql must run on Neon before deploy).
- Batch dropdown (all batches + free-type) and export S.No. grouping: a date-only
  export groups by batch with S.No. reset and a per-group total; a batch-only export
  keeps one continuous S.No.
- Reports redesign: the Machine Performance donut is removed and the Top-5 delay pie
  becomes a full-width horizontal bar chart of every delay type plus a summary table.
- A Production Rate per Hour line chart, batch-driven, hourly from batch start to
  completion by Out Time, zero hours included, midnight-safe.
- Professional Excel formatting on every Downloads sheet (bold highlighted headers,
  highlighted total/summary rows); data, calculations and column order unchanged.

