From 52ff6024e3578c6318f6357a36090e497b3bfe6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:53:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] chromia(qc): fix stuck "Saving...", return to origin view
 with filters, no forced redirects

Saving QC no longer hangs. A server redirect() inside the useActionState action
pinned the button on "Saving..." until a heavy force-dynamic destination finished
rendering, which on a slow render never happened though the save had committed. The
action now returns success and the client navigates, so the button clears the instant
the save commits and cannot be double-submitted.

After saving, QC returns to exactly where the slab was opened from -- the filtered
Slab Records view (filters intact) or Operator Entry -- instead of jumping to
Recalibration/Stockyard. Every outcome returns the same way, Recalibration included;
it no longer redirects to the Recalibration page. QC business logic is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPqDFZ7o6eq1utS7hzoQsF
